                <pb facs="0324" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.24/620a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in El
                        Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-20T16:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1943—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>150. The Coast Guard has been requested by the Salvadoran Military Attaché to
                    sell 1,000 surplus submachine guns to the Salvadoran police.</p>
                <p>Please ascertain very discreetly as much as you can concerning the background and
                    motives of this transaction and report by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
